messages:
jen_support: Received escalation: customer reports streaming API returns truncated JSON (final '}' missing) when using our SSE endpoint, causing client parse failure. Ticket RED-5212, customer blocked.

maria_backend: Can you paste the curl they used?

jen_support: ```bash
curl -N -H "Authorization: Bearer $REDWOOD_KEY" -H "Accept: text/event-stream" -d '{"model":"gpt-open","stream":true,"json":true,"prompt":"..."}' https://api.redwood.ai/v1/streams
```

kevin_sre: Any reverse proxy in front of them? nginx, ALB, env?

jen_support: They said on-prem nginx with proxy_read_timeout 30s. Logs show connection reset ~17s into stream. They provided chunk dump:

```text
data: {"id":1,"text":"{\"items\":[{\"name\":\"a\",\"val\":1},"}
data: {"id":1,"text":"{\"items\":[{\"name\":\"a\",\"val\":1},{\"name\":\"b\",\"val\":2},"}
data: {"id":1,"text":"{\"items\":[{\"name\":\"a\",\"val\":1},{\"name\":\"b\",\"val\":2}]"}
```

maria_backend: Looks like SSE 'data:' lines are splitting JSON fields; final outer '}' missing. Could be our writer emitting partial writes.

oliver_runtime: tagging @eng-runtime. Can you share request-id/timestamps?

jen_support: request id 01HJKLXXXXX, timeframe 2026-11-03T13:45:12Z (unix 1830522312)

ingress-bot: Observability: pool-eu-2 logged connection drop at 2026-11-03T13:45:10Z.

kevin_sre: nginx/proxy config suggestions: proxy_buffering off; proxy_http_version 1.1; proxy_set_header Connection ""; increase proxy_read_timeout.

jen_support: Asked customer to test direct curl from jump host (no proxy) and to provide tcpdump.

jen_support: Customer: "Direct curl from jump host -> still aborts at same point. Tcpdump shows FIN from their proxy to client at 13:45:10, followed by RST from our LB to backend."

maria_backend: Could be regression from SSE framing change. The runtime should emit complete SSE events per token. We'll investigate.

oliver_runtime: Found regression in SSE framing patch (october). Some large events got split across writes causing chunk boundaries inside JSON strings. I'll open PR to revert/fix and backport.

jen_support: Customer asked for workaround. Suggest client-side buffering: accumulate 'data:' lines until empty line then join and parse. Example:

```js
let buf = '';
eventSource.onmessage = (e) => {
  buf += e.data;
  // parse once we detect an event boundary
  try {
    let obj = JSON.parse(buf);
    buf = '';
  } catch (err) {
    // wait for more chunks
  }
};
```

kevin_sre: We'll also recommend disabling proxy buffering and bumping timeouts. Adding those notes to the ticket.

jen_support: Escalating to P1. Ticket RED-5212. Customer in Slack is blocked.

oliver_runtime: PR created: https://github.com/redwood-inference/rt/commit/abc123. Rolling update planned for pool-eu-2 in ~20m.

ingress-bot: Rollout started for pool-eu-2 at 2026-11-03T14:05:00Z.

jen_support: Customer retested — reports final brace present and parses OK. Will monitor 24h then close.

jen_support: Closing note: follow-up action: add additional unit/integration test for SSE atomicity and add telemetry to detect truncated final braces in production streams.

jen_support: Thanks team :thumbsup:
